== no_y
error[Z0401]: `tile` places each mark by its `x` and its `y`, but the plot maps no variable to `y`
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:18
  |
2 | g.plot(x: month).tile()
  |                  ^^^^ needs both `x` and `y`
  |
  = help: map both where the plot starts, as in `plot(x: educ, y: wage)`

== not_a_colour
error[Z0401]: `fill:` of `tile` is "blu", which is not the name of a colour
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:38
  |
2 | g.plot(x: month, y: year).tile(fill: "blu")
  |                                      ^^^^^ not a colour
  |
  = help: did you mean "blue"?

== another_kind_of_fill
error[Z0401]: the plot shows `kind` as categories for `fill`, but `sales`, which `tile` maps to `fill`, is an Int without value labels, which is shown on a continuous scale
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:57
  |
2 | g.plot(x: month, y: year, fill: kind).tile().tile(fill: sales)
  |                                                         ^^^^^ `sales` is of another kind
  |
  = help: the layers of a plot share one scale of fill, so the variables mapped to `fill` must all be categories (a Category, a Str, a Bool or a variable with value labels) or all be numbers without value labels

== a_place_of_another_kind
error[Z0401]: the plot places `year` as categories along `y`, but `sales`, which `tile` maps to `y`, is an Int, which is placed on a linear scale
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:42
  |
2 | g.plot(x: month, y: year).tile().tile(y: sales)
  |                                          ^^^^^ `sales` is of another kind
  |
  = help: the layers of a plot share one axis, so what is mapped to `y` must all be categories (a Str or a Category), all be numbers or all be dates (a Date or a DateTime); `category(v)` makes categories of a number

== alpha_above_one
error[Z0401]: `alpha:` of `tile` is an opacity between 0 and 1, but this is 2
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:39
  |
2 | g.plot(x: month, y: year).tile(alpha: 2)
  |                                       ^ outside [0, 1]
  |
  = help: write 1 for solid tiles, or a share such as 0.5 so that what is under them shows through

== no_color_on_tile
error[Z0404]: `tile` has no argument called `color`
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:32
  |
2 | g.plot(x: month, y: year).tile(color: kind)
  |                                ^^^^^ unknown argument
  |
  = help: usage: `p.tile(data: Frame, x: Var | Expr, y: Var | Expr, fill: Var | Str, alpha: Float = 1)`

== tile_of_a_frame
error[Z0401]: `tile` cannot be called on a Frame
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:1
  |
2 | g.tile()
  | ^ this is a Frame
  |
  = help: `tile` takes a Plot first; `x.tile(...)` is `tile(x, ...)`
